  by centuries of war with the chaos being  severe enough to provide an opening for  none other than Darth Maul to conquer  the planet naturally he uses it as a  headquarters for his criminal syndicates  Sabine Rand one of the main characters  on Star Wars rebels is also a  Mandalorian one who plays an important  part in quoting the society's warring  ways edge of the world during an  interview at the premiere of solo Jon  Favreau and  Hadden explains when the mandalorian is  supposed to take place and the time  period sounds full of opportunity  Favreau explained that the mandalorian  takes place about seven years after  Return of the Jedi or roughly two  decades before the force awakens by this  points the Rebel Alliance has  transformed into the New Republic while  the former Imperials had eventually  formed the first order are still licking  their wounds and the galaxy's Unknown  Regions the Mandalorian is purported to  have a remote setting taking place far  away from the New Republic so it would  be surprised to see any characters from  the movies show up when the Mandalorian  takes place Luke would be busy scouring  the galaxy for for sensitive artifacts  and old Jedi knowledge poe would still  be a kid Finn would be an infant and Rey  wouldn't have even been born yet  one big rebels connection jon favreau is  an adapting Star Wars to the small  screen on his own mission under the  Ironman director is also getting a hand  from a creator some fans will recognize  Dave Filoni he may not be a household  name but if you're a modern-day Star  Wars fan you probably know his work  bologna directed the Clone Wars feature  film which let's face it isn't really  something to brag about  but he also worked side-by-side with  George Lucas to bring the subsequent  superior animated series to the air  fellow knee also co-created both rebels  and the newest Star Wars cartoon  resistance in other words he's the guy  behind a lot of the best parts modern  Star Wars Canon according to the art of  Star Wars the Clone Wars felonious the  brains behind Anakin Skywalker's beloved  apprentice ahsoka tano on rebels for  lonely and his staff raised questions  about the Jedi's relationship with the  force years before the last Jedi he even  voiced chopper rebels scene-stealing  droid  now felonious take on Star Wars - the  Mandalorian sir  he's one of the show's executive  producers and he'll make his live-action  directing debut by helming the  Mandalorians very first episode  the other big rebels connection we're  about to get into spoiler territory if  you haven't seen the series finale of  Star Wars rebels yet you may want to  check out for this part  while the Mandalorian has a title a  premise and the setting in time it still  doesn't have a cast at least not one  that's been announced but we do have  some ideas shortly after the series was  announced a theory emerged that the  mysterious lead character of the  Mandalorian is none other than the  demolitions expert on Star Wars rebel  star Sabine Wren the series ends of  Sabine in ahsoka on a quest to find  throne and  after the fall of the Empire the sort of  mission that could conceivably take  somebody to the very edge of known space  Sabine's got the right ancestry too and  it does seem curious that we haven't  seen our hero's face yet throw in  felonious involvement and the fact that  hey that really could be a woman in  there and you've got a decent argument  that Sabine is the mandalorian of the  series title maybe as a longshot but  what's in store will be exciting to  watch unfold either way we'll find out  more when the series touches down in  2019
 

